<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00005905> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00005905> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-06"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Oxyntomodulin production and secretion by L cells (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "FFAR1/GPR119 -> OXM secretion is IC: OXM rose 5.66x only with combined K-757 (GPR40) + K-833 (GPR119) agonists in humans (PMID:40954563, abstract only); receptor expression in human L cells from RNA-seq (PMID:30733330)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Not modelled: CPE C-terminal trimming, bile acid (CDCA) and lipid/glucose stimulation of OXM (PMID:33459181, 35961260, 27322465), mouse neuromedin C/GRPR stimulation (Grpr is mouse-enriched), OXM in alpha cells/brain."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "OXM enabler = GCG peptide chain UniProtKB:P01275-PRO_0000011255 (aa 53-89). PCSK1->OXM: human organoid PCSK1-/- reduces proglucagon-derived peptides by LC-MS/MS (PMID:36343264); mouse Pcsk1-/- markedly decreases intestinal OXM (PMID:14630721, abstract; ISS)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "OXM->GLP1R from GLP1R-transfected HEK293 cAMP blocked by antagonist (PMID:27322465). OXM also acts on GCGR (not modelled). GLP1R target cell type not specified."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

